#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"the Deutsch and Deutsch-Jozsa algorithms use quantum parallelism combined "
"with interference to find an answer to a problem faster than a classical "
"computer can.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"the phase kickback mechanism is a counterintuitive quantum phenomena that "
"transfers operations on one qubit to the phase of another qubit. The Deutsch"
" and Deutsch-Jozsa algorithms utilize this mechanism.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm offers a polynomial speedup over any "
"deterministic classical algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm can be applied to a different problem, called "
"the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, to find a hidden string encoded in a "
"function.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "True/false {#truefalse}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F Deutsch's algorithm is a special case of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm "
"where the input is a single qubit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F The Deutsch and Deutsch-Jozsa algorithms use quantum superposition and "
"interference to achieve their efficiency.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm requires multiple function evaluations to "
"determine if a function is constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F The \"Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm\" is actually the same as the "
"Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, applied to a different problem.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F The Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm can find multiple secret strings "
"simultaneously.\n"
msgstr ""

